.env
.env.local
.env.*
# The two lines above correctly keep real secrets (.env, infra/.env, any
# .env.local) out of git -- but .env.* also matched .env.example and
# infra/.env.example, the two template files README.md's "Getting
# started" tells a fresh clone to copy from. Neither file was ever
# actually in the repository because of this: `git log --all` has zero
# commits touching either path. Un-ignore them explicitly.
!.env.example
!infra/.env.example
node_modules/

# Go build cache (used for sandboxed builds)
.gocache/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor / OS cruft (defensive -- none currently tracked, keep it that way)
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db

# Go test/coverage artifacts, in case a local `go test -cover` run drops
# one of these inside the tree instead of /tmp
*.test
coverage.out
coverage.html

# Internal working docs from the development/audit process (bug lists,
# gap audits, phased build plans, the pre-build vision doc) -- useful
# during the build, not meant to ship in the judged submission. The
# curated, judge-facing doc set is what README.md's own "Docs" section
# links to (files/AUTH.md, agent-commerce-contract.md, trust-boundary.md,
# pitch-one-pager.md, demo-script.md); none of those are affected. Note:
# dozens of code comments across backend/ and frontend/ still cite these
# filenames (e.g. "PLAN-05-SELLER-DASHBOARD.md §4") as internal design
# notes -- those citations are now unresolvable from inside the repo, a
# deliberate tradeoff for a cleaner file tree.
files/BUGS.md
files/AUDIT-2026-08-29.md
files/REALITY-CHECK-2026-08-30.md
files/ROADMAP-PRIORITIZED.md
files/ORIGINAL-VISION-AUTONOMOUS-REVENUE-AGENT.md
files/ORIGINAL-VISION-BUILD-GUIDE.md
files/PLAN-01-AGENTIC-CORE.md
files/PLAN-02-CATALOG-AND-COMMERCE.md
files/PLAN-03-PROACTIVE-GROWTH-AGENT.md
files/PLAN-04-UI-UX-AND-LATENCY.md
files/PLAN-05-SELLER-DASHBOARD.md
files/PLAN-06-ADDITIONAL-OPPORTUNITIES.md

# Same rationale as above, added later: GIT-WORKFLOW.md documents this
# repo's own internal branch/commit/PR process -- accurate and useful for
# working on this project, but reads as process scaffolding rather than
# submission material, so it moved from the judge-facing set into this
# internal-only list. agent-ai-integration-ideas.md is a brainstorm of
# 10 candidate agent/AI features graded against the real codebase, not a
# claim that all 10 are built -- also internal-only. Both stay on disk
# locally (git rm --cached, not rm); the ~7 code comments citing
# agent-ai-integration-ideas.md by name (e.g. "idea #4 of files/
# agent-ai-integration-ideas.md") become unresolvable-from-outside
# citations, the same accepted tradeoff as the PLAN docs above.
files/GIT-WORKFLOW.md
files/agent-ai-integration-ideas.md
